summary:
scripts/fdev-lane-capacity.py is a read-only probe that prints one JSON line and exits 0 (admit) or 3 (hold). Every condition must hold to admit:

- 5-minute load < max-load-per-core x nproc (default 0.85; benches use 0.25, the FS.GG.Game#780 quiet-host rule that ADR-0098 §4 adopts);
- MemAvailable and any cgroup v2 memory headroom >= 6 GiB; free disk >= 20 GB; /tmp free >= 3 GiB;
- fewer than 2 headless Chromium main processes (children counted once);
- optional max heavy processes.

Lane cgroup quotas lower the effective CPU count and memory headroom. A present but malformed limit file is an unknown: hold, so unknown input never admits. A held probe waits; it is not overridden.

Generic lesson: systems/wip-limits-admission. ADR-0098 §11 tranche 2 (FS-GG/.github#5245) lists this record; the generic technique is a pack entry, the FS-GG instance stays here (§10).
